[ti:Day 17]

[00:00.00]aspect [ˈæspekt]n. (问题、事物等的)方面；情况 例 It is an important aspect of China's trade policy to respect the local custom of the buying country. 搭 from every aspect 从各个方面 / in all aspects 全面
[00:18.12]consult [kənˈsʌlt]vt. 请教，找…商量；咨询；查阅，查 看 vi. 考虑；商议；当顾问 例 The committee does not adequately consult others when drafting amendments. 搭 consult with sb. on sth. 就某事与某人商议
[00:35.28]nominal [ˈnɒmɪnl]a. 名义上的；有名无实的；票面上的 例 The managing director has the nominal power; however, the company is run by his wife.
[00:47.88]hack [hæk]vt. 大量削减；使出租 n. 出租；雇工 a. 出 租的；雇用的 例 The financial budget has been hacked almost in half. 搭 hack writer 雇用文人，御用文人
[01:00.00]forward [ˈfɔːwəd]vt. 促进；发送；发运(商品)，转递(信 件) n. 期货 a. 期货的；预约的 例 Please forward all the letters to me while I'm on holiday. 搭 backward and forward 前后；来回
[01:14.88]admissible [ədˈmɪsəbl]a. 可接受的；可容许的；有资格加入 的 例 It is not admissible that the staff in our company dress in casual clothing during office hours.
[01:29.28]underlying [ˌʌndəˈlaɪɪŋ]a. 优先的；根本的，基础的；潜在的 搭 underlying cause 根本原因
[01:36.48]supplement [ˈsʌplɪmənt]n. 补充；增补；追加；增刊 [ˈsʌplɪment]vt. 增补；补充
[01:43.08]tailor [ˈteɪlə(r)]vt. 剪裁；为特定需要制作；使适应 n. 裁缝 例 The firm can tailor a large order to individual requirements.
[01:54.00]logic [ˈlɒdʒɪk]n. 逻辑学；逻辑性；逻辑 a. 逻辑的 搭 logic design automation 逻辑设计自动化
[02:01.20]rationale [ˌræʃəˈnɑːl]n. 基本原理；理论基础
[02:05.04]affluent [ˈæfluənt]a. 富裕的；富足的 搭 be affluent in 在…方面富足
[02:10.56]certify [ˈsɜːtɪfaɪ]vt. 证明；证明…合格；〈美〉(银行)担 保(支票)可付款 vi. 证明 例 Securities laws currently require research analysts to personally certify that their reports accurately reflect their views of a stock.
[02:30.84]abstain [əbˈsteɪn]vi. 弃权；戒除 例 His decision to abstain from voting faced strong opposition. 搭 abstain from 放弃；戒除
[02:42.24]indispensable [ˌɪndɪˈspensəbl]a. 必不可少的；必需的；责无旁 贷的 例 One of the indispensable functions of an organisation is to promote communication among individuals. 搭 be indispensable for/to 对…是必需的
[03:01.68]surveillance [sɜːˈveɪləns]n. 监视，监督 搭 place sb. under surveillance 把某人置于监督 下
[03:09.60]filibuster [ˈfɪlɪbʌstə(r)]v. 阻碍议案通过；妨碍议事 n. 阻挠 议事的议员；妨碍议事的行动 例 Harry Reid, the majority leader in the Senate, needs 60 votes to break a filibuster.
[03:24.72]existence [ɪɡˈzɪstəns]n. 存在；生存，生活方式 例 The company has gone bankrupt after being an existence for three years. 搭 bring into existence 使产生；使成为 / in existence 存在的；现存的，现有的
[03:41.88]dictaphone [ˈdɪktəfəʊn]n. 录音电话机
[03:45.36]static [ˈstætɪk]a. 静态的；静力的；静电的
[03:48.72]criterion [kraɪˈtɪərɪən]n. (选择、判断等的)标准，准则 例 Establishing criterion for investment of a nation's resources is crucially important for poor countries.
[04:04.44]mutual [ˈmjuːtʃuəl]a. 相互的，彼此的；共同的，共有 的；[保险业]共同承担风险的 搭 mutual effort 共同努力 / mutual trust 相互信 任
[04:14.16]consideration [kənˌsɪdəˈreɪʃn]n. 对价，对偿物；报酬；补偿 金；考虑；体贴，关心 例 Objections to the plan will be taken into consideration. 搭 in consideration of 考虑到，由于；作为对… 的报酬 / leave sth. out of consideration 对某事 不加考虑 / take into consideration 考虑
[04:37.32]reinvest [ˌriːɪnˈvest]vt. 再投资于；(用股息)增购股票 例 He sold his shares and then reinvested the proceeds into other assets. 搭 reinvest sth. into sth. 将…再投资于…派 reinvestment n. 再投资(例：reinvestment of earnings 收益再投资)
[04:58.32]centralise [ˈsentrəlaɪz]vt. 集聚，集中；施行中央集权 vi. 集 中于中央(或中心) 例 The company has built a new headquarters in London to centralise its administration. 搭 centralised operation 集中运作
[05:16.20]telex [ˈteleks] n. 电传；电传打字机
[05:19.08]nullify [ˈnʌlɪfaɪ]vt. 使无效；使无价值；使作废 例 That negative attitude will nullify all the efforts of hunting for a job.
