[07:14.16]federation [ˌfedəˈreɪʃn]n. 联合会；同盟；联邦；联合政府 例 According to the federation rules, all sponsors must remain anonymous for their own protection.
[07:28.80]intangible [ɪnˈtændʒəbl]a. 难以理解的；无形的，触摸不到 的 例 We should try to quantify and measure these seemingly intangible elements.
[07:41.40]prioritise [praɪˈɒrətaɪz]vt. 按优先顺序列出；确定…的优先 次序 例 It was a hard-won opportunity but he had to prioritise his health.
[07:53.28]backbone [ˈbækbəʊn]n. 骨干；支柱；脊柱 例 Now the company has $500 million in annual sales and 4,000 employees and is building much of this country's Internet backbone. 搭 to the backbone 彻头彻尾地
[08:11.76]estimate [ˈestɪmeɪt]v. 估计；估价 [ˈestɪmət]n. 估计；估价 例 They estimate that last year computers sold online were 12% cheaper than in stores. 搭 by rough estimate 粗略估计 / estimate by ratio 按比例估计
[08:30.36]absenteeism [ˌæbsənˈtiːɪzəm]n. (地主、业主)长期在外；旷 工；旷课 例 Finally he was dismissed from his post because of his absenteeism.
[08:42.72]flashy [ˈflæʃi]a. 闪光的；昙花一现的；华而不实的 例 Rather than relying on distracting flashy ads, we developed relevant, clearly marked textbased ads to the right of our search results.
[09:00.24]customise [ˈkʌstəmaɪz]v. 定制，定做；改制 例 He has had his own car customised by request of his daughter.
